# ai-toolkit v2 settings: flat KEY=value (optionally "quoted"), no inline comments, no export.
# Sourced by bash (scripts/lib.sh load_env) and read by Python. Precedence: caller env >
# .ai-toolkit/ai-toolkit.local.env (gitignored, per machine/target) > this file.
SPOKE_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
SPOKE_EFFORT=high
REVIEW_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5
ANSWER_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5
# The model a spoke is relaunched on, once, when its own model stops on a usage limit (#551). Empty = off: the issue is blocked.
FALLBACK_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5
BASE_BRANCH=main
# The project's true main branch, where an issue is done. Empty = BASE_BRANCH: done at land (today). Another branch (an integration BASE_BRANCH, e.g. a protected develop): land.sh still
# pushes BASE_BRANCH, keeps the issue open as status:awaiting-main and opens one rolling PR BASE_BRANCH -> MAIN_BRANCH that humans merge; the merge closes the issues (land.sh --merged).
# LAND_MODE=pr (MAIN_BRANCH empty or = BASE_BRANCH, a protected base): nothing is pushed to the base, each issue becomes its own PR into it.
MAIN_BRANCH=
LAND_MODE=
CHECK_CMD="pytest -n auto tests"
# Per-edit loop (hooks/claude/quality-check.sh): LINT_CMD and TYPECHECK_CMD run on each edited .py file, SHELLCHECK_CMD on each edited shell file (.sh, or a sh/bash/dash/ksh shebang), a failure goes back to the model. Empty = off; the first word is the binary, skipped (never failed) when not installed; no quoting in a knob.
# Override in .ai-toolkit/ai-toolkit.local.env (e.g. TYPECHECK_CMD=mypy). sync.sh proposes ruff.toml / pyrightconfig.json to a Python host that has no such config.
LINT_CMD="ruff check --quiet"
TYPECHECK_CMD=pyright
SHELLCHECK_CMD=shellcheck
CONCURRENCY_CAP=3
GATE_DEFAULT=plan
# Space-separated globs of test files: a commit whose type is not test may not change one (commit-msg hook, rechecked by land.sh). '*' spans '/'. TEST_PATHS= (empty) in
# .ai-toolkit/ai-toolkit.local.env turns the check off for that host.
TEST_PATHS="tests/** test/** **/test_*.py **/*_test.* **/*.test.* **/*.spec.* **/*.bats **/conftest.py"
# 1 = land.sh gates with CHECK_CMD in the spoke instead of CI (until ci.yml exists on the branch; D7).
LOCAL_GATE=0
# A project's command run by land.sh right after the base push, for an issue whose footer says `Tracker: <KEY>`: <cmd> <issue> <key> <sha>, BASE_BRANCH in its environment.
# Empty = nothing runs; a failure only warns and comments on the issue. The command bounds its own run time: land waits for it. Set it in .ai-toolkit/ai-toolkit.local.env.
POST_LAND_CMD=
# A project's command run by dispatch.sh once after a FIRST dispatch of an issue whose footer says `Tracker: <KEY>` (never for --retry-of or --address, so a review round does not run it again): <cmd> <issue> <key>, BASE_BRANCH in its environment.
# Empty = nothing runs; its output goes to stderr and a failure only warns: the worker is started either way. The command bounds its own run time: dispatch waits for it. Set it in .ai-toolkit/ai-toolkit.local.env.
POST_DISPATCH_CMD=
# Where an `away` coordinator loop (coordinator.sh --answer away) POSTs each decision it leaves open (a plan, a permission request, a blocked issue), as ids only. Set it in
# .ai-toolkit/ai-toolkit.local.env (per machine, never synced or committed): it is a secret. Empty = no `away`; a loop started with no --answer runs as away when it is set.
NOTIFY_WEBHOOK_URL=
# With NOTIFY_WEBHOOK_URL set, an `attended` loop also POSTs a decision nobody answered in this many seconds (the delay is checked at the loop's wakes: a minimum): a permission request after
# HANDOVER_PERMISSION_S (the relay denies itself at 540 s, so a value at or above that never fires), a plan or a blocked issue after HANDOVER_PLAN_S. Whole numbers; override per machine.
HANDOVER_PERMISSION_S=300
HANDOVER_PLAN_S=600
# Paid spend (eval draws, model calls, a raised spend cap) the attended and away answerer approves without the human, in whole USD (#550): a plan or round whose whole priced total is below this value is routine
# (the total, not the overrun). 0 or empty = every spend raise goes to the human; an unpriced spend always does. Override per machine or project in .ai-toolkit/ai-toolkit.local.env; a non-number counts as 0.
SPEND_APPROVE_USD=100
ORCA_MIN_VERSION=1.4.246
# owner/repo where tooling defects found in a synced project are filed; sync.sh sets it in a host, empty only in the toolkit itself.
UPSTREAM_REPO=
# Where the toolkit checkout is: sync.sh sets it (in the toolkit itself, its own path). With AUTO_SYNC=1 the coordinator loop syncs its project when that checkout is ahead of
# the installed toolkit-version and then re-executes itself; AUTO_SYNC=0 in .ai-toolkit/ai-toolkit.local.env keeps a project manual.
TOOLKIT_DIR=
AUTO_SYNC=1
# The loop picks and dispatches only open issues carrying this label, and files its own issues with it: on by default, so a repo where others file issues is never dispatched from.
# DISPATCH_LABEL= (empty) in .ai-toolkit/ai-toolkit.local.env opts out: every issue is picked.
DISPATCH_LABEL=ai-toolkit
LANGFUSE_HOST=http://localhost:3000
# The Langfuse key pair is never set here: otel.sh reads the caller env, else the Keychain (services ai-toolkit-langfuse-LANGFUSE_INIT_PROJECT_{PUBLIC,SECRET}_KEY).
# Native OTel export of a spoke (bin/claude-spoke). gRPC and the beta-tracing HTTP port are
# distinct on purpose: a beta endpoint on the normal port silently kills all trace export.
OTEL_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4317
OTEL_BETA_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4418
# The Claude accounts this project may use (#556), in order of preference, space-separated: .ai-toolkit/ai-toolkit.local.env only (per machine, never synced). Empty = the stored login, as today. The first is the default; with 2+ a worker that hits its usage limit is relaunched on the next one that is free.
# The stored login (CLAUDE_STORED_ACCOUNT, default max) needs nothing; any other name needs a full login in the directory ~/.claude-<name> (CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=~/.claude-<name> claude auth login), and is refused without one. No token is ever read or exported.
# A project lists an account only if its data may go through it: a client's account belongs in that client's projects alone.
# CLAUDE_ACCOUNTS="max client"
